<workout_file>
  <name>1:00, 1:30, 2:00, 2:30, 3:00, 3:30, 4:00 - equal work and rest.</name>
  <description>Equal work and rest intervals that increase by 30 seconds each time, working up from 1 minute to 4 minutes.

Concept2 Workout of the Day, 2022-09-11. The archive specifies structure and never
intensity — a WOD says "5 x 4 min / 2 min easy" and leaves the pace to you. The targets here are
derived by Paul's Law from your rowing FTP: shorter pieces harder, longer ones easier. Warm up
before you start; the WOD is the piece, and nothing has been added to it.</description>
  <author>Concept2</author>
  <sportType>rowing</sportType>
  <workout>
    <SteadyState Duration="60" Power="1.52"/>
    <SteadyState Duration="60" Power="0.55"/>
    <SteadyState Duration="90" Power="1.39"/>
    <SteadyState Duration="90" Power="0.55"/>
    <SteadyState Duration="120" Power="1.3"/>
    <SteadyState Duration="120" Power="0.55"/>
    <SteadyState Duration="150" Power="1.25"/>
    <SteadyState Duration="150" Power="0.55"/>
    <SteadyState Duration="180" Power="1.2"/>
    <SteadyState Duration="180" Power="0.55"/>
    <SteadyState Duration="210" Power="1.16"/>
    <SteadyState Duration="210" Power="0.55"/>
    <SteadyState Duration="240" Power="1.13"/>
    <SteadyState Duration="240" Power="0.55"/>
  </workout>
</workout_file>
